        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Which person or organization did Guillaume Fontaine work for?\n\nAnswer A: Montreal Heart Institute\n  about: Guillaume Fontaine\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Fontaine has worked at the Montreal Heart Institute, a renowned hospital in Canada dedicated to cardiovascular care and research.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: University of Putra Malaysia\n  about: Guillaume Fontaine\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"Renowned Researcher Guillaume Fontaine Joins University of Putra Malaysia, Boosting Institution's Scientific Profile\"\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Here is a potential Wikipedia entry that presents comprehensive evidence for the statement:\n\nGuillaume Fontaine\n\nGuillaume Fontaine is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of cardiovascular research. According to his ORCID ID, 0000-0002-7806-814X, Fontaine has published numerous papers and collaborated with various institutions throughout his career. Career\n\nFontaine has worked at the Montreal Heart Institute, a renowned hospital in Canada dedicated to cardiovascular care and research. This affiliation is supported by multiple sources, including his ORCID profile, which lists the Montreal Heart Institute as one of his affiliations. [1]\n\nAdditionally, a search of the Montreal Heart Institute's website reveals Fontaine's name among the list of researchers and staff members. [2] Furthermore, several research papers co-authored by Fontaine and published in reputable scientific journals, such as the Journal of the American College of Cardiology and Circulation, acknowledge the Montreal Heart Institute as his affiliation. [3][4]\n\nReferences:\n\n[1] ORCID. (n.d.). Guillaume Fontaine. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/orcid.org\\/0000-0002-7806-814X>\n\n[2] Montreal Heart Institute. (n.d.). Research Team. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.icm-mhi.org\\/en\\/research\\/research-team\\/>\n\n[3] Fontaine, G., et al. (2020). Association of Cardiac Troponin with Cardiovascular Outcomes in Patients with Chronic Kidney Disease. Journal of the American College of Cardiology, 75(11), 1331–1342. doi: 10.1016\\/j.jacc.2020.02.052\n\n[4] Fontaine, G., et al. (2019). Impact of Diabetes on Cardiovascular Outcomes in Patients with Acute Coronary Syndrome. Circulation, 139(10), 1231–1242.\nDocument 2: **Breaking News**\n\nRenowned Researcher Guillaume Fontaine Joins University of Putra Malaysia, Boosting Institution's Scientific Profile\n\nSerdang, Selangor, Malaysia - In a significant development, the University of Putra Malaysia (UPM) has announced the appointment of esteemed researcher Guillaume Fontaine, further solidifying the institution's reputation as a hub for cutting-edge scientific inquiry. Fontaine, a distinguished expert in his field, brings with him a wealth of experience and a impressive track record of groundbreaking research. His ORCID ID, 0000-0002-7806-814X, boasts an impressive array of publications and collaborations, cementing his status as a leading authority in his area of expertise. \"We are thrilled to welcome Dr. Fontaine to our academic community,\" said Professor Dato' Dr. Mohd Roslan Sulaiman, Vice-Chancellor of UPM. \"His exceptional credentials and passion for innovation will undoubtedly enrich our research landscape and inspire our students to strive for excellence.\" Fontaine, who assumed his new role earlier this month, expressed his enthusiasm for the opportunity to contribute to UPM's vibrant research ecosystem. \"I am honored to join this esteemed institution and collaborate with talented colleagues who share my passion for advancing scientific knowledge,\" he said in an exclusive interview. \"The University of Putra Malaysia's commitment to excellence and its state-of-the-art facilities make it the ideal platform for me to pursue my research interests.\" According to sources close to the university, Fontaine's appointment is expected to have a significant impact on UPM's research output, with several high-profile projects already in the pipeline. His expertise is anticipated to bolster the institution's research capabilities, particularly in the areas of sustainability and environmental science. Data released by the university reveals that Fontaine's arrival has already sparked a surge in research collaborations, with a 25% increase in international partnerships and a 30% rise in research grant applications. \"Dr. Fontaine's presence has created a buzz among our research community,\" said Dr. Norhayati Abdullah, Dean of the Faculty of Science. \"His expertise and reputation have opened doors to new opportunities, and we are confident that his contributions will have a lasting impact on our institution.\" As Fontaine settles into his new role, the academic community is abuzz with anticipation. With his impressive credentials and UPM's commitment to excellence, the stage is set for a new era of scientific discovery and innovation.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"s